// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b44-b4
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "b440.1" source="b440" target="SNOMED_CT:78064003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b440 SNOMED CT 78064003 (Respiration functions) = ICF b440: the body functions of
        respiration/breathing, including b4400 respiratory rate, b4401 respiratory rhythm, b4402
        respiratory depth. Target =, active RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT observable that
        captures respiration-as-a-function and is the closest standard equivalent of ICF b440; its
        parent is 3709003 is 246464006 grouping, and its siblings/valued correlates include 45804006,
        86290005 (b4400), 48064009 (b4401). Broader rather than exact only because ICF b440 is a
        multi-child function block (b4400-b4402) where the SNOMED CT concept is a single flat observable,
        and ICF uses (Andningsfunktioner) vs SNOMED CT. High tier : direct term-and-scope match
        (respiratory function = respiration functions) verified active in the mirror, but
        one-level-broader in model granularity with no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b440-b449.1" source="b440-b449" target="SNOMED_CT:78064003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b440-b449 SNOMED CT 78064003 = ICF block b440-b449 Respiration functions: the block-level
        grouping of respiration functions (b440) AND respiratory muscle functions (b445). Target =,
        active. No single SNOMED CT block observable exists; the nearest standard ancestor that contains
        the respiration-function core of this block is 78064003. Broader (moderate): a block-level
        respiration+respiratory-muscle grouping mapped up to the respiratory-function observable is a
        deeper climb than the b440 map, and the target covers the b440 respiration axis fully but the
        b445 respiratory-muscle axis only partially (SNOMED CT has no dedicated respiratory-muscle-function
        observable, only 73898009 32058005), so 78064003 is the nearest defensible ancestor and the
        dominant axis. Per the rubric, the moderate tier applies for this best-available but looser
        block-level map.
        """
}
mapping "b4400.1" source="b4400" target="SNOMED_CT:86290005" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4400 SNOMED CT 86290005 (Funktioner för andningsfrekvens) = ICF b4400 Respiration rate
        functions: the respiration sub-function of the rate (breaths per unit time) of breathing. Target
        =, active RF2 production. Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical concept (respiratory rate as
        a respiration function), confirmed by literal term match; ICF (respiration rate) = SNOMED CT. The
        SNOMED CT concept is the direct functional observable whose parent is 250810003 271625008 364063000
        is inactive/D. exact_match: same concept, term-verified active.
        """
}
mapping "b4401.1" source="b4401" target="SNOMED_CT:48064009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4401 SNOMED CT 48064009 (Funktioner för andningsrytm) = ICF b4401 Respiration rhythm
        functions: the respiration sub-function of the rhythmic pattern of breathing (regularity and
        timing of the breathing cycle). Target =, active RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT
        function observable that names respiratory rhythm as a function; it is the functional observable
        where 5467003 is its valued correlate, and 248582003 is the sibling assessment-axis observable.
        Broader rather than exact: ICF b4401 (respiration rhythm) and are denotationally the same
        clinical concept, but the SNOMED CT concept is modelled as a single flat function observable
        against ICF's multi-aspect rhythm function (regularity, pattern, timing), so one-level-broader
        in model granularity. High tier : direct term-and-scope match (respiratory rhythm =
        andningsrytm) verified active in the mirror, but one-level-broader with no independent
        crosswalk. (248582003; 48064009 chosen as it is the explicit function observable, matching the
        ICF function framing.)
        """
}
mapping "b4402.1" source="b4402" target="SNOMED_CT:271626009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4402 SNOMED CT 271626009 (Funktioner för andningsdjup) = ICF b4402 Respiration depth
        functions: the respiration sub-function of the depth (tidal volume / amplitude) of breathing.
        Target =, active RF2 production. This is the only active SNOMED CT observable that names the
        depth-of-respiration axis; the legacy 7808001 is inactive/D (valid_end 2006-07-31). Broader
        (moderate): 271626009 is the depth-of-respiration assessment observable (the best available
        active standard concept), but it is not modelled as an explicit observable (the function-framed
        concept was retired), so the target captures the same clinical axis but as a generic observable
        rather than a function. Per the rubric, the moderate tier applies for this best-available but
        looser (function-retired) map.
        """
}
assessment "b4408.omop" source="b4408" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b4409.omop" source="b4409" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b445.1" source="b445" target="SNOMED_CT:3709003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b445 SNOMED CT 3709003 = ICF b445 Respiratory muscle functions: the body functions of the
        muscles used for breathing, including b4450 thoracic respiratory muscles, b4451 diaphragm, b4452
        accessory respiratory muscles. Target =, active RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT
        function observable that captures breathing-movement-as-a-function and is the closest standard
        equivalent of ICF b445; it is the parent observable of 78064003 are 271620003, 1119516004. No
        dedicated observable exists in SNOMED CT (252486000 is a *procedure*, 32058005 is the reflex not
        the function). Broader rather than exact: 3709003 denotes respiratory *movement* as a function,
        which is the breathing-movement product of the respiratory muscles (the b445 function), but it
        models the movement not the muscles-as-such, so one-level-broader in scope. High tier : the
        closest defensible respiratory-muscle function observable, term-verified active, but
        one-level-broader with no independent crosswalk.
        """
}
mapping "b4450.1" source="b4450" target="SNOMED_CT:264825005" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4450 SNOMED CT 264825005 = ICF b4450 Functions of thoracic respiratory muscles: the
        respiratory-muscle sub-function of the thoracic cage muscles (intercostals, etc.) used in
        breathing. Target =, active RF2 production. No dedicated observable exists in SNOMED CT: the
        candidate 252486000 is a procedure, and the function hierarchy has no thoracic-muscle-specific
        function observable. 264825005 is the only SNOMED CT observable that names the chest/thoracic
        respiratory-movement axis directly. Related rather than exact/broader: 264825005 is the
        observable of chest respiratory *movements* (the movement product), not the physiological
        *function* of the thoracic respiratory muscles — the SNOMED CT function hierarchy does not model
        thoracic-respiratory-muscle function separately. Low tier : the closest defensible
        thoracic-respiratory observable, term-verified active, but a movement-vs-function model mismatch
        and no independent crosswalk.
        """
}
mapping "b4451.1" source="b4451" target="SNOMED_CT:111969002" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4451 SNOMED CT 111969002 = ICF b4451 Functions of the diaphragm: the respiratory-muscle
        sub-function of the diaphragm (the primary breathing muscle). Target =, active RF2 production,
        whose parent is 8690003. No dedicated observable exists in SNOMED CT: the candidate 413983009 /
        413984003 are device observables; 111969002 is the only active SNOMED CT observable that names the
        diaphragm-as-breathing axis. Related rather than exact/broader: 111969002 is the observable of
        diaphragmatic *movement* (the movement product of diaphragm contraction), not the physiological
        *function* of the diaphragm — the SNOMED CT function hierarchy does not model diaphragm function
        separately. Low tier : the closest defensible diaphragm observable, term-verified active, but a
        movement-vs-function model mismatch and no independent crosswalk.
        """
}
mapping "b4452.1" source="b4452" target="SNOMED_CT:73898009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4452 SNOMED CT 73898009 = ICF b4452 Functions of accessory respiratory muscles: the
        respiratory-muscle sub-function of the accessory breathing muscles (sternocleidomastoid,
        scalenes, pectoralis) recruited in laboured breathing. Target =, active RF2 production. This is
        the direct SNOMED CT function observable that names accessory-muscle respiratory movement as a
        function; its valued correlate is 271620003. Broader (moderate): 73898009 captures the
        accessory-muscle respiratory-movement axis (the clinical core of ICF b4452) and is the closest
        standard equivalent, but it models the *movement* product rather than the muscles-as-a-function
        explicitly; one-level-broader than an exact function-framed match. Per the rubric, the moderate
        tier applies for this best-available but looser map. (162895003 considered and rejected:
        inactive/D, and a finding not a function.)
        """
}
assessment "b4458.omop" source="b4458" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b4459.omop" source="b4459" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b449.omop" source="b449" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b450.1" source="b450" target="SNOMED_CT:78064003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b450 SNOMED CT 78064003 = ICF b450: the ICF block of (b4500-b4509), grouping the subsidiary
        respiratory-function children: mouth breathing (b4500), cough (b4501), sneeze (b4502), yawn
        (b4503), functions related to respiratory mucus (b4504). Target =, active RF2 production, the
        direct SNOMED CT observable capturing respiratory-system functions overall. This is the closest
        standard equivalent of the ICF b450 grouping; it sits above the b4500-b4504 children in the
        observable hierarchy. Broader rather than exact only because ICF b450 is a multi-child function
        block (b4500-b4509) where is a single flat observable, and the ICF block bundles several
        sub-functions (cough/sneeze/yawn/mucus) that SNOMED CT models as separate findings/observables
        rather than under one concept. High tier : direct term-and-scope match (respiratory function =
        additional respiratory functions) verified active in the mirror, but one-level-broader in model
        granularity with no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
assessment "b450-b469.omop" source="b450-b469" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b4500.1" source="b4500" target="SNOMED_CT:77329001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4500 SNOMED CT 77329001 = ICF b4500: the body function of breathing through the mouth (the
        respiratory sub-function of mouth breathing, distinct from nasal breathing). Target =, active
        RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT concept that names mouth breathing; sibling concepts
        (110289004, 110290008 due to nasal obstruction, 110291007 chronic) are its qualified variants.
        Broader rather than exact: SNOMED CT models mouth breathing as a FINDING (a clinical observation)
        whereas ICF b4500 frames it as a FUNCTION (the physiological act); the finding concept fully
        contains the source domain but is modelled one level away as an observation rather than as the
        function itself, and there is no SNOMED CT observable. High tier : direct term-and-scope match
        (mouth breathing = function of breathing through the mouth) verified active in the mirror, no
        independent Athena crosswalk re-verified, one-level-broader in model framing.
        """
}
mapping "b4501.1" source="b4501" target="SNOMED_CT:49727002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4501 SNOMED CT 49727002 = ICF b4501: the body function of coughing (the respiratory
        protective/reflex sub-function of producing a cough). Target =, active RF2 production, the
        canonical SNOMED CT concept naming cough (valued correlates 11833005 dry, 28743005 productive,
        43025008 paroxysmal sit beneath). This is the closest standard equivalent; SNOMED CT also has
        34606001 (the function framing), but 49727002 is the dominant, clinically used concept for cough
        as a function/act. Broader rather than exact: SNOMED CT models cough as a FINDING (clinical
        observation) where ICF b4501 frames it as a FUNCTION (the physiological reflex/action); the
        finding concept fully contains the source domain but is one level away in model framing. High
        tier : direct term-and-scope match (cough = function of coughing) verified active in the mirror,
        no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified, one-level-broader in model framing. (34606001; the
        finding is preferred as the primary clinical concept.)
        """
}
mapping "b4502.1" source="b4502" target="SNOMED_CT:76067001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4502 SNOMED CT 76067001 = ICF b4502: the body function of sneezing (the respiratory
        protective/reflex sub-function of producing a sneeze). Target =, active RF2 production, the
        canonical SNOMED CT concept naming sneezing. This is the closest standard equivalent; no dedicated
        observable exists in the mirror (unlike cough, which has 34606001). Broader rather than exact:
        SNOMED CT models sneezing as a FINDING (clinical observation) where ICF b4502 frames it as a
        FUNCTION (the physiological reflex/action); the finding concept fully contains the source domain
        but is one level away in model framing. High tier : direct term-and-scope match (sneezing =
        function of sneezing) verified active in the mirror, no independent Athena crosswalk
