        """
}
mapping "b4503.1" source="b4503" target="SNOMED_CT:37993006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4503 SNOMED CT 37993006 = ICF b4503: the body function of yawning (the respiratory/reflex
        sub-function of producing a yawn). Target =, active RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT
        OBSERVABLE that names yawning AS A FUNCTION — the closest framing to ICF's function perspective;
        sibling findings (248626009, 301250005, 191957001) are observation/valued concepts. Broader
        rather than exact: ICF b4503 is the yawning function generally where 37993006 denotes the
        function observable; one-level-broader in model granularity and there is no independent Athena
        crosswalk re-verified. High tier : direct term-and-scope match (yawning function = function of
        yawning) verified active in the mirror, the function-oriented observable (preferred over the
        finding per the b310 voice-function precedent).
        """
}
mapping "b4504.1" source="b4504" target="SNOMED_CT:3371003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b4504 SNOMED CT 3371003 = ICF b4504: the body functions related to respiratory mucus
        (production AND transport of airway secretions, with sub-children b45040 production, b45041
        transport, b45048 other, b45049 unspecified). Target =, active RF2 production. This is the only
        SNOMED CT function-observable in the mirror that names the mucociliary transport mechanism (the
        ciliary action that transports mucus); no SNOMED CT or observable exists (sputum appears only as a
        substance 45710003 or as cough-up findings). Broader rather than exact: 3371003 denotes ONLY the
        ciliary-action/transport axis of mucus handling and does not name the production axis that b4504
        also covers — it is one axis of a two-axis source, which would normally be, but as the SINGLE
        best target it stands broader for the transport component (production has no defensible standard
        target and is left implicit). Low tier : the closest defensible mucus-related function
        observable, term-verified active, but the target covers only the transport/ciliary sub-axis of
        the broader b4504 mucus-function block, and there is no independent crosswalk. A single
        partial-with-no-companion target usually caps at, but the transport-axis containment is
        defensible and 3371003 is the unambiguous standard observable for the dominant mucus-transport
        function, so a low-tier broader map is justified over a weak/partial or no_match.
        """
}
assessment "b45040.omop" source="b45040" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b45041.1" source="b45041" target="SNOMED_CT:3371003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b45041 SNOMED CT 3371003 = ICF b45041: the specific body function of TRANSPORT of
        respiratory mucus (mucociliary clearance — the ciliary action and mucus escalator that moves
        airway secretions up and out). Target =, active RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT
        function-observable that names the ciliary-action mechanism responsible for mucus transport, and
        is the closest standard equivalent of the ICF mucus-transport function. Broader rather than
        exact: ICF b45041 frames mucus transport as a function (covering ciliary action PLUS the
        mucus-rheology/cough-assisted components of clearance) where 3371003 denotes specifically the
        ciliary-action axis; the target fully contains the ciliary-transport core of the source but the
        ICF concept is slightly broader than ciliary action alone. Moderate tier : direct term-and-scope
        match on the ciliary-transport mechanism, term-verified active, but one-level-broader in scope
        and no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
